<title>SINGAPORE: Taiwan's CPS buys term fuel oil at plus $28.60/T.</title>
<headline>Taiwan's CPS buys term fuel oil at plus $28.60/T.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Taiwan state oil company, Chinese Petroleum Corp (CPC) has awarded six-month term tender to buy low sulphur fuel oil at $28.60 per tonne premium to Singapore spot quotes on a cost-and-freight basis, a company official said on Friday.</p>
<p>Under the tender, which closed April 24 and was valid until April 25, CPC will take delivery of a 38,000 tonne cargo of low pour low sulphur fuel per month between June and November.</p>
<p>The cargoes are for delivered to the ports of Keelung, Shen Ao or Taichung.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65-870-3082)</p>
</text>
